WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
A ROOM MODEL IS NOT EVIDENCE. A fictional room can expose assumptions without claiming how a real person will respond.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.000
DECLARE THE VARIABLES. Light, sound, layout and nature are model inputs—not measured causes or effects.

3
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.000
CHANGE THE FICTIONAL CONTEXT. When room or goal changes, recompute only the declared tradeoff model.

4
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.000
SHOW WHAT IS UNKNOWN. Real exposure, people, responses, accessibility and competing needs remain unmeasured.

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.000
MODEL ≠ MEASUREMENT ≠ PRESCRIPTION. An illustrative score cannot become a health, performance or design conclusion.

6
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.000
MAKE THE ASSUMPTIONS VISIBLE. Use the model to form questions for real evidence and affected people.
